Package: cybroid-edition-network
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: CybroidOS maintainers <citos@cybroid.com>
Homepage: https://cybroid.com/cybroidos
Section: metapackages
Priority: optional
Depends: cybroid-plasma (>= @VERSION@), wireshark, tshark, nmap, zenmap, tcpdump, iperf3, mtr-tiny, traceroute, arping, fping, hping3, arp-scan, iftop, nethogs, ethtool, iw, wavemon, lldpd, speedtest-cli, putty, telnet, sshpass, expect, tftpd-hpa, tftp-hpa, dnsmasq, filezilla, remmina, snmp, ipcalc, sipcalc, frr, vpcs, python3-scapy, python3-netmiko, python3-paramiko, ansible
Description: CybroidOS Network: for network engineers and students
 The tools network engineers use: Wireshark, Nmap with Zenmap, tcpdump,
 iperf3, mtr, traceroute, fping, hping3, arp-scan; PuTTY for serial
 consoles, SSH and Telnet; MikroTik's WinBox; bandwidth monitors (iftop per
 host, nethogs per program) and Wi-Fi tools (iw, wavemon); a TFTP server
 for device configs and firmware, dnsmasq for lab DHCP and DNS; FileZilla
 and Remmina; SNMP tools and subnet calculators; FRRouting and VPCS for
 practice; and Ansible, Netmiko, Paramiko and Scapy for automation. Pairs
 with the CIT platform's network labs.
 .
 The same CybroidOS as every edition (look, updates, Hangar), with these
 tools added. Chosen in the welcome at first sign-in, or later in Settings
 (any number of editions together), and installed from deb.cybroid.com.
